# Clean Code: Code Hygiene and Pragmatic Rules

## Delete Dead Code

Never comment out code "for later." Version control preserves history. Dead code creates confusion about what's active.

```
// BAD - Commented code clutters and confuses
function calculateTotal(items) {
    // const subtotal = items.reduce((a, b) => a + b.price, 0)
    // const tax = subtotal * 0.08
    // return subtotal + tax
    return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price * 1.08, 0)
}

// GOOD - Clean, only active code
function calculateTotal(items) {
    return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price * 1.08, 0)
}
```

## No Magic Numbers or Strings

Extract literals into named constants that explain their purpose.

```
// BAD - What do these numbers mean?
if (retryCount > 3) { }
await sleep(86400000)
if (status === 'A') { }

// GOOD - Self-documenting constants
const MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS = 3
const ONE_DAY_MS = 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000
const STATUS_ACTIVE = 'A'

if (retryCount > MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS) { }
await sleep(ONE_DAY_MS)
if (status === STATUS_ACTIVE) { }
```

## Comment Discipline

Default stance: **minimize comments.** Well-named functions, variables, and clear structure should make code self-documenting.

**Do NOT:**
- Add inline comments that narrate what the next line does ("Get the user", "Check if valid")
- Add JSDoc/JavaDoc that merely restate the method signature
- Add class or module header comments that repeat the class name

**When comments ARE valuable:**
- Business rules, regulatory or compliance reasons
- Non-obvious workarounds or "why not the obvious approach"
- Links to external references (tickets, RFCs, specs)

```
// GOOD - Comment explains why (business context)
// Users inactive for 90+ days lose premium status per policy update 2024-03
if (daysSinceLastLogin > 90) {
    revokePremiumStatus(user)
}
```

## Fail Fast

Validate inputs at system boundaries. Throw errors early rather than propagating bad state.

```
// BAD - Error surfaces far from cause
function processOrder(order) {
    // ... 50 lines of processing ...
    sendEmail(order.customer.email)  // NullPointerException here!
}

// GOOD - Validate upfront
function processOrder(order) {
    if (order == null) throw new Error("Order is required")
    if (order.customer?.email == null) throw new Error("Customer email is required")
    
    // Safe to proceed
}
```

## Pragmatic Rules

### Rule of Three

Don't abstract prematurely. Wait until you see a pattern three times before extracting.

1. First occurrence: Just write it
2. Second occurrence: Note the duplication, but tolerate it
3. Third occurrence: Now refactor — you understand the pattern

### Avoid Premature Optimization

Write clear code first. Optimize only when you have evidence of a performance problem.

> "Premature optimization is the root of all evil." — Donald Knuth

### Let Tools Handle Formatting

Configure automated formatters and linters once, then forget about it. Use your language's standard formatter; run formatting on save or pre-commit.

